          "bug_bounty_scope": "in-scope",
          "notes": "Attacker includes non-empty ommers list in a post-merge block. If not validated, this violates the PoS invariant."
        },
        "test_procedure": "1. Identify the block validation entry point in the P2P message handler where incoming blocks are deserialized.\n2. Craft a post-merge (Osaka fork) block with a non-empty ommers list in the block body.\n3. Submit the malformed block via P2P network protocol and observe the validation response.\n4. Verify the block is rejected with an appropriate error code before further processing.\n5. Confirm the ommers_hash header field is validated to equal EMPTY_OMMER_HASH.\n6. Check that no partial state changes occur from processing the invalid block.\n7. Review error handling to ensure no information leakage about internal validation logic.",
        "bug_class": "Input Validation",
        "risk_category": "Tampering",
        "notes": "Source: PROP-W7B16-16, Trust Boundary: tb-001, Invariant: SG-004/INV-004, Threat: stride-010",
        "code_scope": {
          "locations": [
            {
              "file": "beacon-chain/blockchain/execution_engine.go",
              "symbol": "notifyNewPayload",
              "line_range": {
